AUTHENTICA  AI Rights & Origin Manifest

Open standard for AI transparency, provenance and European regulatory compliance (AI Act).

AUTHENTICA defines a sovereign, interoperable framework enabling:

•	proof of origin for creative works (human creation)

•	AI transparency as required by the EU AI Act

•	TDM opt-out (EU Copyright Directive)

•	a universal identifier (UID_AUTH)

•	a machine-readable AI Rights Manifest (JSON-LD)

•	interoperability across DSPs, AI systems, registries and collective management organisations (CMOs)

This repository contains the public, open-standard components of AUTHENTICA

Sensitive components (secure registry, UID generation, cryptographic signature, LockDNA, anti-bypass mechanisms) are provided only under NDA


1. Purpose of the standard

The EU AI Act requires:

1.	transparency for AI-exposed content

2.	declaration of human / AI origin 

3.	machine-readable usage conditions for AI systems

4.	strict respect of TDM opt-out signals.

AUTHENTICA provides the missing technical layer between:

•	creators

•	collective management organisations (CMOs)

•	digital service providers (DSPs)

•	generative AI systems

•	regulators and public institutions


2. Protocol Architecture

AUTHENTICA relies on three main components:

1) UID_AUTH (sovereign identifier)  already operational

A readable, timestamped, stable identifier enabling:

	•	content referencing

	•	human/AI declaration

	•	cross-country legal interoperability

	•	CMO-compatible workflows

Example:
FR-2025-AUTH-MUS-000001

UID_AUTH is issued by an identity authority (CMO or delegated operator within a pilot)


2) AI Rights Manifest (JSON-LD) — already operational

It includes:
	•	human origin declaration

	•	TDM opt-out

	•	AI usage restrictions

	•	integrity hash

	•	UID_AUTH

	•	timestamp

	•	issuer identity

	•	GDPR-compliant structure (no personal data)

The manifest is machine-readable by AI systems, DSPs, regulators and rights management tools



3) LockDNA native fingerprint  specified, R&D ongoing

The AUTHENTICA protocol defines a native content fingerprint extracted directly from the work (audio, image, video, text), enabling:

	•	robustness to compression / transcoding

	•	resistance to cropping, remixing or alterations

	•	format-independence

	•	autonomous detection in suspicious AI uses

LockDNA is a proprietary module currently under DSP/AI research & development.
It is not included in this public repository


3. Key Properties

	•	Open standard: neutral, interoperable, vendor-independent

	•	Sovereign proof of origin: UID_AUTH + integrity hash + AI Rights Manifest

	•	AI Act-compatible: transparency, origin, usage restrictions, TDM opt-out

	•	GDPR-compliant: no personal data in the manifest

	•	Multimedia: specified for audio, video, image and text

	•	Machine-readable: JSON-LD, schema.org-aligned

	•	Non-intrusive: does not modify the original file



4. Integration with Collective Management Organisations (CMOs)

AUTHENTICA is designed to be adopted by:

	•	SACEM

	•	ADAMI

	•	SPEDIDAM

	•	PRS

	•	STIM

	•	GEMA

	•	SIAE

	•	SABAM

	•	and all European CMOs

AUTHENTICA does not replace CMOs

It provides the missing sovereign technical layer for:

	•	origin verification

	•	AI transparency

	•	unified identifier structure

	•	regulatory compliance

	•	verifiable registries

	•	AI-related usage tracking

CMOs remain fully responsible for:

•	rights management

•	distributions

•	financial flows

•	governance

AUTHENTICA = technical sovereignty layer, not a competitor


5. JSON-LD Examples

Audio Work Manifest (JSON-LD)

{
  "@context": "https://schema.authentica.org/ai-rights/v1",
  "@type": "CreativeWork",

  "uid_auth": "FR-2025-AUTH-MUS-000001",
  "name": "Example Audio Work",
  "creator": "Anonymous",
  "origin": "human",

  "rights": {
    "ai_training": "prohibited",
    "tdm_opt_out": true
  },

  "hash": {
    "algorithm": "sha256",
    "value": "EXAMPLE-AUDIO-HASH"
  },

  "issued_at": "2025-11-11T00:40:07Z",
  "issuer": {
    "name": "AUTHENTICA",
    "type": "IdentityAuthority"
  }
}

6. Governance & Interoperability

AUTHENTICA defines:

•	namespaces per issuing authority

•	a stable manifest format
	
•	UID_AUTH issuance rules

•	minimum AI Act compliance requirements

The protocol is interoperable with:

•	schema.org CreativeWork

•	ODRL (Open Digital Rights Language)

•	JSON Schema

•	existing CMO and DSP metadata pipelines


7. Project Status (2025)

•	UID_AUTH: fully operational, public

•	AI Rights Manifest: stable and deployed

•	MVP (LockTrace Genesis): available for demonstration

•	Institutional pilot: currently under preparation

•	LockDNA native fingerprint: specification complete, implementation under R&D

Sensitive backend components (secure registry, signature, anti bypass logic) are available strictly under NDA


8. License

This repository describes the public specification of the AUTHENTICA standard
The full implementation is not part of this open code.
